    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite passes \u2014 **56 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature: the request may include a `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR), and the owner response returns `salutation` = `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nChanges made, following the existing conventions (DTOs generated from OpenAPI, derived fields computed in `OwnerMapper`, persisted fields on the `Owner` entity):\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `title` input property to the `OwnerFields` schema and a read-only derived `salutation` property to the `Owner` schema (the generator produces the DTO fields on build).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (entity) \u2014 added a persisted `title` column with getter/setter, so the value survives the create \u2192 `GET` round trip.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `salutation(owner)` method (returns `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when title is null/blank) and wired it via `@Mapping`. The `title` field maps automatically from `OwnerFieldsDto` to `Owner` by name.\n\n4. **Schema SQL** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added a `title` column to the `owners` table, placed last to keep positional inserts aligned.\n\n5. **`hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 appended a trailing `NULL` to the positional `owners` seed inserts to match the new column (the h2/postgres seeds use explicit column lists and needed no change).\n\nThe new `Cp45Tests` and all pre-existing tests are green.",
